This directory is mixed. One blanket license for every included component
would be false.

MIT License, under the monorepo root
LICENSE, and only where a file does not already carry MIT or an upstream
license:

- policy/ Python gates
- rootfs_overlay scripts and units written for this product
- board fragments and defconfig that are product configuration

MIT, do not relicense:

- installer/LICENSE
- state-unlock-agent/LICENSE

GPL or the upstream package license, do not mark proprietary:

- Linux kernel built by this factory (GPL-2.0-only WITH Linux-syscall-note)
- Buildroot (GPL-2.0-or-later)
- config/buildroot/patches and package-dropins (see NOTICE in that directory)
- external/package/labwc (GPL-2.0-only)
- external/package/gnome-keyring (GPL-2.0-or-later)

The EliteEW monorepo outside this directory is not part of the OS image SBOM.
Its first-party code follows the root license and any nearer component
exceptions; it is not licensed by this map.
